      "text": "To determine the perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) in the right prism with an equilateral triangle base, we first need to find the coordinates of points \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\). We start by placing the equilateral triangle \\(ABC\\) in the coordinate plane.\n\nSince the side length of the equilateral triangle is 12, we can place the vertices of the triangle as follows:\n- \\(A = (0, 0)\\)\n- \\(B = (12, 0)\\)\n- \\(C = (6, -6)\\)\n\nNext, we find the coordinates of points \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\), which are the midpoints of edges \\(AC\\), \\(BC\\), and \\(DC\\) respectively:\n- \\(X\\) is the midpoint of \\(AC\\):\n  \\[\n  X = \\left( \\frac{0+6}{2}, \\frac{0-6}{2} \\right) = (3, -3)\n  \\]\n- \\(Y\\) is the midpoint of \\(BC\\):\n  \\[\n  Y = \\left( \\frac{12+6}{2}, \\frac{0-6}{2} \\right) = (9, -3)\n  \\]\n- \\(Z\\) is the midpoint of \\(DC\\):\n  \\[\n  Z = \\left( \\frac{6+0}{2}, \\frac{-6-6}{2} \\right) = (3, -6)\n  \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the lengths of the sides of triangle \\(XYZ\\). The coordinates of \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\) are:\n- \\(X = (3, -3)\\)\n- \\(Y = (9, -3)\\)\n- \\(Z = (3, -6)\\)\n\nThe distance formula between two points \\((x_1, y_1)\\) and \\((x_2, y_2)\\) is given by:\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we calculate the length of \\(XY\\):\n\\[\nXY = \\sqrt{(9 - 3)^2 + (-3 - (-3))^2} = \\sqrt{6^2 + 0^2} = \\sqrt{36} = 6\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the length of \\(XZ\\):\n\\[\nXZ = \\sqrt{(3 - 3)^2 + (-6 - (-3))^2} = \\sqrt{0^2 + (-3)^2} = \\sqrt{9} = 3\n\\]\n\nFinally, we calculate the length of \\(YZ\\):\n\\[\nYZ = \\sqrt{(9 - 3)^2 + (-3 - (-6))^2} = \\sqrt{6^2 + 3^2} = \\sqrt{36 + 9} = \\sqrt{45} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nThe perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) is the sum of the lengths of its sides:\n\\[\n\\text{Perimeter} = XY + XZ + YZ = 6 + 3 + 3\\sqrt{5} = 9 + 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nThus, the perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{9 + 3\\sqrt{5}}\n\\]",
